  "question": {
    "text": "A spherical chocolate ball has a layer of ice-cream of uniform thickness around it. When the thickness of the ice-cream layer is 1 cm , the ice-cream melts at the rate of $81 \\mathrm{~cm}^3 / \\mathrm{min}$ and the thickness of the ice-cream layer decreases at the rate of $\\frac{1}{4 \\pi} \\mathrm{~cm} / \\mathrm{min}$. The surface area (in $\\mathrm{cm}^2$ ) of the chocolate ball (without the ice-cream layer) is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$196 \\pi$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$256 \\pi$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$225 \\pi$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$128 \\pi$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0010_43eb09445dc3.png\"><br>\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{v}=\\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\mathrm{r}^3 \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{dv}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=4 \\pi \\mathrm{r}^2 \\frac{\\mathrm{dr}}{\\mathrm{dt}} \\\\\n& 81=4 \\pi \\mathrm{r}^2 \\times \\frac{1}{4 \\pi} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{r}^2=81 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{r}=9\n\\end{aligned}$\nsurface area of chocolate $=4 \\pi(r-1)^2=256 \\pi$"
  }
